{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And He poured upon him.</b> Like \"a charming step upon him\" (Genesis 49:22) — upon each of our fathers:" "<b>Wrath.</b> And it is 'the wrath of His anger,' like 'the tent that was his mother's' (Genesis 24:47):" "<b>And it consumed him round about.</b> From the root of להט החרב (Genesis 3:24), and behold they shall acknowledge that their fathers were blind of heart, so that they did not know:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads the suffix in Genesis 49:22 as referring to Jacob's sons rather than Joseph."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:39.239137929Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}